1
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,880
(Longfan Urban Construction General Manager
Huo Qicheng Found Dead)

2
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,830
Ming, are you there?

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,910
Are you there, Ming?

4
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:15,910
Captain Qin, I'm here.

5
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:18,510
That's great.

6
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:20,320
It's nothing urgent.

7
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,960
I just wanted to ask you something.

8
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:24,640
How did you know

9
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:28,000
there was a bomb in Car 6 of K5289?

10
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:30,760
In the original 1990 timeline,

11
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:33,000
you died in that bombing.

12
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:34,030
Later,

13
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:36,000
the news reports
mentioned those details.

14
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:37,920
Wait. Let me get this straight.

15
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,150
I was supposed to

16
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,150
die in that bombing,

17
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,430
but you sent me a warning

18
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:48,070
from the future and saved me.

19
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:51,030
Then where am I in 2020?

20
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,600
I changed history.

21
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:56,560
The future has already changed.

22
00:00:56,670 --> 00:00:57,470
In my original memories,

23
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:59,110
you were absent
from all those important moments,

24
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:00,640
but now you're there.

25
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,480
At the same time,

26
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,680
a murder case that never happened before

27
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:09,950
appeared in the 1990 cold case files.

28
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,710
The victim

29
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:13,760
was Huo Qicheng,

30
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,310
General Manager
of Longfan Urban Construction Group.

31
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,920
I was in charge of Huo Qicheng's case.

32
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:23,350
How did it become a cold case by 2020?

33
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:25,400
Did I fail to solve it?

34
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:27,350
I changed history,

35
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,760
but now I don't know
where history is headed.

36
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:31,950
Let me... Let me get this straight.

37
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,070
So,

38
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:34,710
before I survived,

39
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,840
this case never existed.

40
00:01:36,950 --> 00:01:38,280
It only happened

41
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:40,560
after I survived.

42
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,680
Did my survival
somehow cause this murder?

43
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:45,790
It wasn't you.

44
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:47,230
It was me.

45
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,480
I opened Pandora's box

46
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:52,280
and unleashed a terrifying killer.

47
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:53,560
I saved you,

48
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,000
but I got someone else killed.

49
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,710
Dad.

50
00:01:58,590 --> 00:01:59,950
But I still want to save you.

51
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,790
I thought if I saved you,

52
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,510
I'd get to see you in 2020.

53
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,640
But I didn't.

54
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,840
All that happened was more murders,

55
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,030
and you still didn't make it to 2020.

56
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,360
But right now, I still don't know

57
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,520
what else might happen.

58
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,280
If I can change the past
from the future,

59
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:26,960
maybe you can change
the future from the past.

60
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,800
Son.

61
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,120
You're right about that.

62
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,120
I'm a police officer.

63
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:36,560
Even if you opened Pandora's box,

64
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:38,560
no matter how many killers
you unleashed,

65
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:42,080
I'll catch every last one
of them for you.

66
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:42,910
Dad.

67
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:44,870
I'm a police officer too.

68
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:47,360
When I was little, you promised me

69
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,520
we'd catch killers together.

70
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,150
Now,

71
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,030
we finally can.

72
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:58,620
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 3=

73
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:09,710
Qin.

74
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:11,630
The autopsy is complete.

75
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:14,190
We can confirm the time
of death was 10:30 PM.

76
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,590
The cause of death is very clear.

77
00:03:15,710 --> 00:03:17,030
Severe traumatic brain injury.

78
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:18,310
The murder weapon
was a round-headed hammer.

79
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:20,710
There were no other
significant findings.

80
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:22,430
Wait a minute.

81
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:26,710
What are these marks around the wound?

82
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,190
They look like pressure marks.

83
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:29,240
Qin.

84
00:03:29,590 --> 00:03:31,030
Modern forensic medicine emphasizes that

85
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:33,360
any contact can leave a trace.

86
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:35,400
The body can tell you who the killer is.

87
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,080
Pay close attention

88
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,870
to highly pliable tissues like the skin.

89
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:39,680
With blunt force trauma,

90
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,870
especially repeated overlapping blows,

91
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,680
a masking effect can occur,

92
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,680
causing the initial
or less severe injuries

93
00:03:45,710 --> 00:03:48,470
to be obscured or destroyed by later,
more severe trauma.

94
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,080
I've reviewed Huo Qicheng's case file.

95
00:03:51,630 --> 00:03:52,800
His autopsy report

96
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,710
didn't mention

97
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:55,560
any injuries associated
with the sequence of blows.

98
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:36,680
Dad.

99
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,680
Dad.

100
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,390
Son.

101
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:12,750
Dad.

102
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,560
There's something I forgot to tell you.

103
00:05:15,390 --> 00:05:17,480
We should focus on examining

104
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,830
the relatively intact skin
around the wounds,

105
00:05:18,830 --> 00:05:19,800
especially over bone-supported areas

106
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,360
like the temporal bone
and the edge of the jaw,

107
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:23,160
to see if there are impressions
different from the hammer's surface.

108
00:05:23,310 --> 00:05:25,630
Those could be the killer's signature.

109
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,360
Dad.

110
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,390
Did you hear what I said?

111
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:34,070
I did.

112
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,480
Then, according to what you said,

113
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,240
if the killer didn't want
blood splattering everywhere

114
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:44,360
or wanted to muffle the sound
of the hammer blows,

115
00:05:44,950 --> 00:05:46,190
what would he do?

116
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:51,070
He'd wrap something
around the hammerhead

117
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:54,240
or around the victim's head

118
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:57,160
to cushion the blows.

119
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:57,920
Exactly.

120
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,430
Like this?

121
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,430
Here, let's try it.

122
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,240
Dad, stop messing around.

123
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:14,480
Yes, that's right.

124
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:15,830
Dad.

125
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:16,950
Put your clothes back on.

126
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:17,390
Okay.

127
00:06:55,070 --> 00:06:56,630
I brought back
several types of raincoats

128
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,240
available on the market.

129
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,800
No.

130
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,240
This plastic one

131
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:02,430
has a completely smooth surface.

132
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:03,720
There's no texture at all.

133
00:07:03,830 --> 00:07:04,870
It's obviously not right.

134
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:11,950
This one

135
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:13,920
isn't right either.

136
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,560
This is oilcloth.

137
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:16,950
It does have some texture,

138
00:07:16,950 --> 00:07:18,120
but it's too fine.

139
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,510
It doesn't match.

140
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:27,680
Li, don't move.

141
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:32,160
Nylon. This looks promising.

142
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:33,870
Let's see.

143
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:39,560
Turn around. Hold that position.

144
00:07:46,310 --> 00:07:48,360
Qin, this is it.

145
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:51,830
The texture and spacing
are an exact match.

146
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:52,830
They match the pressure marks.

147
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,560
We can confirm

148
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:56,870
the killer used

149
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:58,430
a raincoat made
of this type of nylon as padding.

150
00:07:58,430 --> 00:07:59,190
Are you sure?

151
00:07:59,190 --> 00:07:59,680
I'm sure.

152
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,390
Li.

153
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,750
Is this type of raincoat
common on the market?

154
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:03,510
Is it expensive?

155
00:08:04,070 --> 00:08:05,240
It's not that common.

156
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:07,800
The material only came out
in the last few years.

157
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,920
It's less stuffy than nylon

158
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,120
and even lighter.

159
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,240
It's still not widely used.

160
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,390
In that case,

161
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,720
let's go back to the area
around the villa

162
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:17,120
and see if we can find
any witnesses from that night.

163
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,070
Don't move yet.

164
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:25,040
I'll have Medical Examiner Zhou
take a few photos of you.

165
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,240
Captain Qin, how long do I
have to stay like this?

166
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,510
Captain, when are we leaving?

167
00:08:32,670 --> 00:08:34,200
Zhou, hurry up with those photos.

168
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,550
I can't hold this pose much longer.

169
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:43,550
Cap... Captain.

170
00:08:43,550 --> 00:08:45,000
Do I... Do I still have
to hold this pose?

171
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,000
Captain.

172
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:51,200
Captain.

173
00:08:54,630 --> 00:08:55,440
Hello.

174
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:58,600
What can I do for you two?

175
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,440
We're from the Public Security Bureau.

176
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:02,650
(Qin Tian)
We'd like to ask you a few questions.

177
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:03,390
(Wang Li)

178
00:09:03,390 --> 00:09:06,480
Do you remember
the heavy rain last Wednesday?

179
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,480
Why are you asking?

180
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,550
Just answer the question.

181
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:11,720
What's with you?

182
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:13,200
What's with that attitude?

183
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,510
Is that how you ask someone questions?

184
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:16,150
I remember that day.

185
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:17,600
I happened to be on the night shift.

186
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,150
Then do you remember

187
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:23,000
anything unusual happening

188
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:24,670
at your complex or nearby,

189
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:26,840
or anyone acting suspiciously?

190
00:09:27,030 --> 00:09:28,320
Nothing suspicious.

191
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,480
Oh, now I remember.

192
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:34,600
I did see Li Daguo that day,

193
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:38,030
wandering around the complex

194
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,840
in a tattered raincoat.

195
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,080
He had this blank stare.

196
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,000
It gave me quite a fright.

197
00:09:42,630 --> 00:09:43,600
You mean...

198
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:44,550
Li Daguo.

199
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,150
The one from the steel mill up ahead.

200
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:48,440
I live around there too.

201
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,790
He's pretty well known
in our neighborhood.

202
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,960
But later, because of
the Urban Construction Group,

203
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,150
he was cheated out of a lot of money.

204
00:09:55,910 --> 00:09:57,440
He used to be a very honest man.

205
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,870
Now, trying to get his money back

206
00:09:59,270 --> 00:10:00,670
has left him like a man possessed.

207
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:03,030
Do you know his exact house number?

208
00:10:03,030 --> 00:10:05,440
I'm really not sure
about his house number.

209
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,200
What a waste of time.

210
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,960
What's with you?

211
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,390
Li Daguo.

212
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,030
Li Daguo.

213
00:10:30,870 --> 00:10:32,750
Are you looking for Daguo?

214
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,550
Did something happen to him?

215
00:10:36,550 --> 00:10:37,000
Madam.

216
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,720
We're here to ask Li Daguo
to assist with an investigation.

217
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:41,080
Do you know if he's home?

218
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:42,550
Daguo has really

219
00:10:43,150 --> 00:10:44,510
been through so much.

220
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:47,440
You mean the Longfan Urban Construction
Fundraising Case, right?

221
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:51,030
That Huo Qicheng was a terrible man.

222
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,200
They swindled Daguo
out of everything he had.

223
00:10:53,510 --> 00:10:55,480
He even got several
coworkers he was close to

224
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,630
to invest too.

225
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:58,120
And now,

226
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,320
he's lost everything,

227
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,630
and so have his coworkers.

228
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:03,510
They come to his door every day,

229
00:11:03,510 --> 00:11:04,790
calling him a fraud

230
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,960
and an accomplice of Huo Qicheng.

231
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:11,480
All that turmoil

232
00:11:12,150 --> 00:11:13,630
literally drove his mother to her death.

233
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:17,200
A few days ago, after Daguo finished
arranging his mother's funeral,

234
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:19,320
he grabbed a hammer

235
00:11:19,630 --> 00:11:21,720
and went after Huo Qicheng.

236
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:23,840
Everyone managed to stop him.

237
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,910
It's been quiet
these past few days, though.

238
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,510
Officers,

239
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,720
he's not home.

240
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:34,630
He may have gone
into hiding from his creditors.

241
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,670
The poor boy.

242
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,870
He knows I'm getting old,

243
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,670
so he's always
helping me with little things.

244
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,910
I wish you could help him.

245
00:11:46,030 --> 00:11:46,910
I have

246
00:11:48,030 --> 00:11:50,080
a spare key to his place.

247
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,120
Thank you, madam.

248
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:53,910
Thank you.

249
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:54,720
Sorry for the trouble.

250
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,960
Stop coming here.

251
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,600
I don't have any money to pay you back.

252
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,960
Calm down, Li Daguo.

253
00:12:37,150 --> 00:12:38,360
We're from
the Criminal Investigation Unit.

254
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:40,270
We need you to assist us with a case.

255
00:12:40,270 --> 00:12:41,200
It's about Huo Qicheng.

256
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:45,860
(Fundraising Fraud Victim, Li Daguo)

257
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:55,000
I did it.

258
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:56,510
Li Daguo.

259
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,750
Do you know what you're saying?

260
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,720
I killed him.

261
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,150
I used that hammer to kill him.

262
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,150
Did you kill Huo Qicheng?

263
00:13:12,030 --> 00:13:12,840
Yes.

264
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,600
Why did you kill him?

265
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:17,390
He swindled me out of all my money,

266
00:13:18,390 --> 00:13:19,840
took all my coworkers' money,

267
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:21,670
and caused my mother's death.

268
00:13:23,030 --> 00:13:24,360
Didn't he deserve to die?

269
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,480
Tell us how you committed the crime.

270
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,440
That rainy night,

271
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,030
I went to his house.

272
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,030
I climbed over the wall to get in.

273
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:36,030
He was asleep in bed at the time.

274
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,080
I hit him with a hammer

275
00:13:39,550 --> 00:13:40,390
over and over.

276
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,840
What were you wearing
when you went to his house?

277
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:44,440
A raincoat.

278
00:13:44,790 --> 00:13:46,200
And when you struck him with the hammer,

279
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,080
how did you do it?

280
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:48,360
What do you mean?

281
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,320
What else was I supposed to do?

282
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:57,240
His blood spurted out immediately.

283
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,390
It splattered all over my face.

284
00:13:59,870 --> 00:14:00,870
Never in my life

285
00:14:01,550 --> 00:14:02,960
had I felt so relieved.

286
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,440
I beat him to death.

287
00:14:06,150 --> 00:14:08,360
Beat him to death!

288
00:14:08,550 --> 00:14:09,550
Beat him to death!

289
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:15,030
Captain Qin, the test results are back.

290
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,360
The hammer from your house

291
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,870
has been tested.

292
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,550
The dark red substance
on the hammer isn't human blood.

293
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:32,510
It's paint.

294
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:34,600
Also,

295
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,120
no traces of blood

296
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,630
were found
in the crevices of the hammer.

297
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:44,480
The hammer from your house
isn't the murder weapon.

298
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,600
You don't even know
how the crime was actually committed.

299
00:14:46,870 --> 00:14:48,840
You're giving false testimony.
Do you understand?

300
00:14:49,270 --> 00:14:50,320
That's against the law too.

301
00:14:57,550 --> 00:14:58,630
Then what am I supposed to do?

302
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,670
That man is dead now.

303
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:03,600
The money is gone.

304
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:06,720
All my coworkers'
hard-earned money is gone.

305
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:10,510
Zhang's son needs money for surgery.

306
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:12,840
Wang's wedding has fallen through too.

307
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,200
They all come to me.

308
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:19,030
I was the one who assured them
they'd make money.

309
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,550
I ruined everything for them.

310
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:26,840
I want to end it all too!

311
00:15:32,790 --> 00:15:34,120
It's hell out there.

312
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:40,200
It's hell in here too.

313
00:15:42,550 --> 00:15:44,750
Can't you just say I killed him?

314
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,910
Just execute me and put an end to it!

315
00:15:49,510 --> 00:15:50,750
Then it'll all be over.

316
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,360
I'll confess.

317
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,870
I killed him.

318
00:15:58,910 --> 00:16:00,080
I killed him!

319
00:16:18,030 --> 00:16:18,840
Qin.

320
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,150
How's it going in there?

321
00:16:20,630 --> 00:16:21,750
I was just about to report to you.

322
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:22,790
Well...

323
00:16:24,630 --> 00:16:25,440
Zhuang.

324
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:26,630
It's clean enough in here now.

325
00:16:26,630 --> 00:16:27,670
That's all for today.

326
00:16:27,670 --> 00:16:28,630
Go home and get some rest.

327
00:16:34,790 --> 00:16:36,120
I'll head home, then.

328
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,120
I'll come back tomorrow.

329
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:37,750
Okay.

330
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:38,600
Thanks for your hard work.

331
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,390
Chief.

332
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,270
What's going on?

333
00:16:52,030 --> 00:16:52,840
Didn't Zhuang's daughter

334
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,790
die in the train bombing?

335
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:56,440
He was grieving
at home and couldn't bear it,

336
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:58,080
so he wanted to find some work
to keep his mind occupied.

337
00:16:58,080 --> 00:17:00,320
We happened to need someone
to clean the bureau,

338
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,390
so I asked him to come help out

339
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:02,720
and earn a little extra for the family.

340
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,510
Chief,

341
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:05,830
Zhuang looks like
he's really struggling.

342
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:08,200
Why don't we take up
a collection for him?

343
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,240
Qin.

344
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:12,070
What do you think?

345
00:17:12,070 --> 00:17:13,240
Should I organize a collection?

346
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,720
If you do, include Li Daguo too.

347
00:17:14,830 --> 00:17:15,750
Well, you...

348
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,070
He's in a bad mood.

349
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:18,960
Chief.

350
00:17:19,270 --> 00:17:21,830
Make sure you let me know
when you collect the donations.

351
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,000
Sure.

352
00:17:23,110 --> 00:17:24,240
I'll let you know.

353
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,510
The Rainy Night Hammer
Killer Case spans 30 years

354
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,590
and remains unsolved to this day.

355
00:17:33,350 --> 00:17:35,110
Now we've found a pile of human remains.

356
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,110
What other connection do those two have
with Longfan Urban Construction Group

357
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,350
besides what we already know?

358
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:42,920
This case

359
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:45,590
was never supposed to exist.

360
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,440
What do you mean?

361
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,110
If I hadn't changed history,

362
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:51,580
(Huo Qicheng)
he wouldn't have died.

363
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:53,400
What did you say?

364
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:55,000
Who... Who wouldn't have died?

365
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,450
I have something to take care of.

366
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:57,510
I'm leaving.

367
00:18:06,030 --> 00:18:08,160
Someone who usually sleeps
in the autopsy room

368
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,070
is leaving this early today?

369
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:11,750
Does he have something going on?

370
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,270
Probably not.

371
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,750
Hasn't he always been like this?

372
00:18:15,750 --> 00:18:16,920
Always acting mysterious.

373
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:20,830
Captain Qin.

374
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:22,960
Now it's your turn.

375
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:25,000
It all started with you.

376
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:27,310
And it must end with you.

377
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,000
Qin.

378
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,400
Qin, are you okay? Qin.

379
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:41,590
Answer me if you can hear me, Qin.

380
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:43,750
Qin.

381
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:44,790
Qin.

382
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,000
Qin.

383
00:18:46,270 --> 00:18:47,440
Can you hear me, Qin?

384
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:57,080
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

385
00:19:00,150 --> 00:19:04,930
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

386
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:13,020
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

387
00:19:13,550 --> 00:19:18,880
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

388
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:28,870
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

389
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:34,550
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

390
00:19:36,590 --> 00:19:44,900
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

391
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:50,750
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

392
00:19:52,210 --> 00:20:00,330
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

393
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:06,060
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

394
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:15,880
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

395
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:23,430
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

396
00:20:23,630 --> 00:20:28,040
♪Can you hear me?♪

397
00:20:28,050 --> 00:20:31,840
♪Can you hear me?♪

398
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:39,300
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

399
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:47,040
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

400
00:20:47,370 --> 00:20:52,980
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

401
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:58,460
♪After all these years♪

402
00:21:00,970 --> 00:21:08,450
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

403
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:10,650
♪And tell you♪

404
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:15,140
♪I haven't let you down♪
